WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.682
This example shows a small analytics class called SalesReport.

00:00:04.682 --> 00:00:07.782
The class stores a list of sales values.

00:00:07.782 --> 00:00:12.572
Then it provides methods that calculate summary information about those values.

00:00:12.572 --> 00:00:16.372
The total_sales method returns the sum of all sales.

00:00:16.372 --> 00:00:19.542
The average_sale method calculates the average.

00:00:19.542 --> 00:00:25.662
The high_sales_count method counts how many sales values are greater than or equal to a cutoff.

00:00:25.662 --> 00:00:31.162
This is a useful class example because the data and the calculations belong together.

00:00:31.162 --> 00:00:37.632
The sales list is stored inside the object, and the methods describe actions related to that list.

00:00:37.632 --> 00:00:42.912
After defining the class, we create a report object with five sales values.

00:00:42.912 --> 00:00:48.342
Then we print the total sales, average sale, and the number of sales at least 200.

00:00:48.342 --> 00:00:50.812
Run the code and inspect the output.

00:00:50.812 --> 00:00:55.392
Then change the cutoff from 200 to 150 and run it again.

00:00:55.392 --> 00:00:59.912
The high sales count should change because the rule became easier to meet.

00:00:59.912 --> 00:01:04.358
This example shows how a class can organize a small reporting workflow.
